1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,964
This November,

2
00:00:00,964 --> 00:00:03,443
book authors start collecting from a

3
00:00:03,443 --> 00:00:06,335
1.5 billion dollar AI copyright settlement

4
00:00:06,335 --> 00:00:07,368
with Anthropic.

5
00:00:07,368 --> 00:00:08,342
In June 2025,

6
00:00:08,342 --> 00:00:10,440
the judge drew a sharp line:

7
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:12,763
training AI on bought books was

8
00:00:12,763 --> 00:00:13,437
fair use,

9
00:00:13,437 --> 00:00:16,585
but downloading millions of pirated copies

10
00:00:16,585 --> 00:00:17,184
was not.

11
00:00:17,184 --> 00:00:18,176
Before trial,

12
00:00:18,176 --> 00:00:21,688
Anthropic settled without admitting liability,

13
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:25,123
covering 482,460 registered books from LibGen

14
00:00:25,123 --> 00:00:27,795
and PiLiMi at roughly 3,000 dollars

15
00:00:27,795 --> 00:00:29,016
gross per title.

16
00:00:29,016 --> 00:00:31,719
Across 77 tracked AI data disputes,

17
00:00:31,719 --> 00:00:34,500
that 1.5 billion dollar fund remains

18
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:37,512
the largest copyright payout on record.

19
00:00:37,512 --> 00:00:38,514
For builders,

20
00:00:38,514 --> 00:00:40,134
pay for clean inputs.

21
00:00:40,134 --> 00:00:41,136
For creators,

22
00:00:41,136 --> 00:00:44,529
timely copyright registration was the ticket

23
00:00:44,529 --> 00:00:45,840
into this payout.
